                <pb facs="0500" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/487: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-28T12:00:00-05:00">November 28,
                        1929—noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>394. Associated Press despatch from Moscow printed in today’s papers say China
                    has accepted Russian terms for settlement Chinese Eastern Railway controversy.
                    Can you confirm?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
